findings.body:
**Issue:** Every request Origin is echoed as `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` while `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials` is always `true`. Any malicious site can make credentialed cross-origin calls and read the API response (session cookies / auth the browser attaches automatically).

**Failure mode:** Attacker page at `https://evil.example` sends a credentialed `fetch` to this API. The browser includes the victim’s cookies; this middleware returns `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: https://evil.example` + credentials, so the attacker script can read the body.

**Fix:** Keep an explicit allowlist. Extend it only with known mobile WebView origins if needed. CORS does not apply to pure native HTTP clients — do not open reflection for them.

```suggestion
  const ALLOWED = new Set(["https://app.example.com"]);
  if (origin && ALLOWED.has(origin)) {
    return {
      "Access-Control-Allow-Origin": origin,
      "Access-Control-Allow-Credentials": "true",
      Vary: "Origin",
    };
  }
  return { Vary: "Origin" };
```
